# Keep the GYSH guide tabs

The live site lost Prerequisites / Tools / Pricing / Steps when a checkout without `GuidePrepSections.tsx` was deployed. Cloudflare `--branch=main` is only a label. It does not mean git `main`.

Before any GYSH `git checkout`, `git switch`, or `npm run deploy:pages`:

- `side-hustle-hub/src/components/GuidePrepSections.tsx` must exist.
- `StepByStepGuides.tsx` must render `<GuidePrepSections`.
- `functions/_lib/stripe.ts` must define `resolveChargeablePriceId`.
- `functions/_lib/stripe-checkout.ts` must call it. A catalog price id goes stale when Stripe deactivates that Price. Checkout has to use the active Price for the lookup key, or the inactive-price error returns.

If the target branch or working tree fails that check, do not switch and do not deploy. Bring the guide-tab files onto the branch first.

`deploy-pages.mjs` aborts when `scripts/gysh-deploy-guard.mjs` reports the tabs are missing. Do not bypass that guard, and do not run `wrangler pages deploy` by itself.

Uncommitted files are uploaded (`--commit-dirty=true`). A stash is not. Confirm the stash is not the only copy of work you still need before deploying.
